{"EmbeddableHost.before_validation calls self.host.sub! without nil guard, raising NoMethodError when host is nil": 0.9427626729011536, "Admin::EmbeddableHostsController#update does not guard against nil when fetching host by id, causing NoMethodError when host.save is called on nil": 0.8884406685829163, "Admin embedding REST adapter's pathFor() always returns /admin/customize/embedding, causing REST calls intended for /admin/embeddable_hosts to be silently routed to the wrong endpoint": 0.5886834263801575, "EmbeddableHost component uses decorator syntax (@on, @observes, @computed) which requires specific Babel/Ember build configuration for stage-2 decorators support, risking build failures or runtime errors": 0.2941947877407074, "DB-backed embeddable host allowlist blocks all embedding for non-admins when EmbeddableHost table is empty, with no fallback to old site_setting-based list": 0.5255966186523438, "Migration creates embeddable_hosts table and migrates data from site settings with risk of data loss, mis-mapped categories, and rollback complexity": 0.6297072172164917, "Host allowlist check in topic_retriever.rb depends on EmbeddableHost.host_allowed? with no fallback if embeddable_hosts table is empty": 0.35544461011886597, "Admin UI saveChanges calls embedding.update({}) but Admin::EmbeddingController#update only re-serializes without persisting changes, making the save action a no-op": 0.7233732342720032, "EmbeddingSerializer uses embed: :ids and EmbeddableHostSerializer only exposes category_id, causing N+1 requests when UI fetches category data separately": 0.38770797848701477, "TopicEmbed.import uses eh.try(:category_id) which may be nil when no EmbeddableHost matches the URL, potentially causing post creation failure or unexpected default category": 0.8278812766075134, "Routes expose both customize/embedding and resources :embeddable_hosts creating overlapping contract surfaces that diverge from Ember REST adapter's path resolution": 0.41801443696022034, "Removal of old SiteSetting.allows_embeddable_host? tests creates coverage gaps for edge cases like nil/malformed hosts": 0.8569682836532593}